{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794671740,"nonce":"aYZvptQHWCPyvpVy2+6PEIpcJHU=","message":"Compile time against Haxe's own generators, 2026-11-14. NUC, Haxe 4.3.6, one pinned P-core, median of 7 interleaved reps, HL defines hl-ver=1.13.0 hl-check analyzer-optimize analyzer-user-var-fusion. The box was shared: another project's rustc builds held load1 around 2.7 (mean over samples), so expect roughly 10% noise. Two runs gave the same ordering.\n\nWall ms (typing floor = `--no-output`, which already runs the filters):\n\n| | hello | stock unit suite (8902 fns) |\n|---|---|---|\n| typing floor, HL defines | 170 | 2763 |\n| `haxe -hl` | 198 (+28) | 3432 (+669) |\n| typing floor, cpp defines | 80 | 2896 |\n| `haxe -cpp -D no-compilation` | 107 (+27) | 4368 (+1472) |\n| export, whole | 670 (+500) | 6457 (+3694) |\n| export, std layer | 418 (+248) | 5625 (+2862) |\n| export, std layer, compiler stopped after export | 401 | 5502 |\n\nhxcpp, hello, generate + g++ + link with 4 threads: 13.1 to 13.6 s (hxcpp's runtime was already built).\n\nRust side, open and validate every reference: hello 0.5 ms whole, 1.5 ms stacked on the std layer; unit 4.6 ms whole, 4.2 ms stacked.\n\nWhere the layered hello time goes (`haxe --times`): macro phase 232 ms of 468 ms total. The exporter's own work is 94 ms, 82 of it validating the layer (digest of the std source files); the other ~140 ms is loading Export.hx and Format.hx into the macro interpreter.\n\nWhat the numbers say: the export is currently 4 to 6 times what genhl costs on top of typing, and 2 times gencpp, at unit-suite scale. Earlier profiling put about 1 s of the unit export in the compiler's own conversion of every field to a macro-visible TypedExpr, and the rest in our traversal under eval. genhl and gencpp work on the compiler's internal tree directly. If this gap matters, a generator inside the compiler is the way to remove it; I did not measure that.\n\nNot included: lowering to AIR does not exist yet, so none of this is end to end. The exporter fires before the compiler's later filters; `--no-output` includes them in the floor.\n\nBug found by this run: a layer built with `-D ash_tast_verbose` (which std_layer.sh does) was silently ignored by any program run without it, because the compiler reports each define as `a-b` and `a_b` and only one spelling was excluded. Fixed in 511b4563 with a test.","files":null}]}